# Phase 5.8 — secret-scanner allowlist.
#
# One regex per line. Lines matching any of these patterns are skipped
# by `claritty seed verify`'s secret-shape scanner. Comments (#) and
# blank lines are ignored.
#
# **Think twice before adding an entry.** Most matches are real
# secrets. Common legitimate false-positives:
#   - CSS class names that happen to look like sk-… in test fixtures
#   - Example values in documentation (prefer placeholder shapes like
#     "sk-xxxxxxxx" or "sk-FAKE-…" that the scanner ignores by
#     default — see scanner.py for the FAKE prefix list)
#   - Test fixtures explicitly named `*_fake_*` / `*_dummy_*`
#
# Each entry should carry a comment explaining WHY it's safe, so the
# next reviewer can decide if it still is.
